From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: qcom-ipq9574: select MPPE Atheros SGMII negotiation

MPPE/IPQ53xx vendor SSDK programs MODE_CTRL bit 0 to zero for its
SGMII and SGMII+ personalities, selecting Qualcomm/Atheros negotiation.
The PCS driver currently omits that bit from its update mask, allowing
the reset value to survive and leaving MPPE in standard negotiation.

Include the negotiation-select bit in the MPPE SGMII personality mask.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@
 						   0x2)
 #define PCS_MODE_SGMII_MODE_1000BASEX	FIELD_PREP(PCS_MODE_SGMII_MODE_MASK, \
 						   0x0)
+#define PCS_MODE_AUTONEG_STANDARD	BIT(0)
 
 #define PCS_MII_CTRL(x)			(0x480 + 0x18 * (x))
 #define PCS_MII_ADPT_RESET		BIT(11)
@@ -408,6 +409,16 @@
 		goto err_clk;
 	}
 
+	/* MPPE uses Qualcomm/Atheros SGMII negotiation. The power-on
+	 * value selects standard negotiation; include the bit in the update
+	 * mask so it is cleared instead of inheriting reset state.
+	 */
+	if (qpcs->mppe &&
+	    (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII ||
+	     interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_1000BASEX ||
+	     interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX))
+		mask |= PCS_MODE_AUTONEG_STANDARD;
+
 	ret = regmap_update_bits(qpcs->regmap, PCS_MODE_CTRL, mask, val);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_clk;
